  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 259 PM CDT Sat Apr 18 2026\n\nA shortwave embedded in the flow aloft will move over our area late \nSunday night into Monday morning, followed by another late Monday \nnight into Tuesday. With return low-level southerly flow and \nincreased moisture, showers and thunderstorms will be possible.\nThe more substantive rainfall looks to be with the first system late \nSunday night into Monday morning. Temperatures are expected to stay \ncool and well-below normal on Monday, with highs limited to the \nupper 50s and lower 60s in our southern and central counties, and \nmid/upper 60s in the Big Country.  \n\nWeak shortwave ridging aloft over our area Wednesday will be \nfollowed by quasi-zonal flow Thursday into next weekend, while a \nlarge upper trough progresses from the western CONUS across the \nnorthern and central Plains. The low-level setup will feature \nincreased south winds in our area with a tightened pressure \ngradient. Lee surface trough/dryline will be over West Texas \nWednesday afternoon, and in the far northwestern part of our area to \nfar northwestern Crockett County Thursday afternoon. Our area will \nhave warm and more humid conditions in that time frame, and higher \ninstability is progged ahead of the dryline. May have a weak cold \nfrontal passage on Friday, but this looks to be mainly a wind shift \nwith drier air advecting into the area.",
